	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relative Humidity} is the ratio of the partial pressure of water vapor in an air-water mixture to the saturated vapor pressure of water at a prescribed temperature. The relative humidity of air depends not only on temperature but also on the pressure of the system of interest. Relative Humidity is also referred to as \\text{Relative Partial Pressure. Relative partial pressure is often referred to as (RH) and expressed in percent."@en .
